%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...Thanks.\d%K%P
「…对不起」%K%P
Yeah, I guess even I would be bothered by a huge, useless\npiece of furniture frozen in the fetal position in the\nmiddle of my room as it exuded an aura of bleak abjection.%K%P
在房间正中，有个巨大的物体，\n正抱着膝盖向四面八方发散着黑暗，\n这对别人来说毫无疑问会感觉郁闷之至吧。%K%P
Yet Ms. Kaya still kept treating this oversized piece of\ngarbage like it was worthy of compassion, even offering to\naddress it with human words.%K%P
然而夏夜小姐，对这种只会麻烦别人的废物，\n还能用温柔的语气与之交谈。%K%P
The amount of problems I imposed on her bordered on the\nridiculous.%K%P
明明我添的麻烦，\n可以说已经达到不成体统的程度了。%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dAh, I'm partly responsible for this too, you know. I'm\nsorry. I kinda started bullying her before I realized it.\d%K%P
「啊～，我也有责任。\n抱歉啊。不知不觉就开始欺负她了」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dNo, it's not your fault, Ms. Kaya. This is all my\nresponsibility to bear.\d%K%P
「不，夏夜小姐没有错。\n全都是我的错」%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dWell, duh, of course it's all your fault.\d%K%P
「那倒是，全都是因为理君」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...That's true, but I would appreciate some civility for\na change.\d%K%P
「…话是这么说，\n不过还是用委婉一点的说法吧」%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dI'm pretty sure you're mistaken about exactly how you're\nresponsible, though. I'd stake my life on it.\d%K%P
「问题就是关于你的责任是什么，\n我想你对这个的认识绝对有错误」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dEh...?\d%K%P
「诶…？」%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dWell, I guess spelling it out would be in poor taste.\d%K%P
「不过把那个说出来就不知趣了吧…」%K%P
I had no idea where she was heading with this, but\napparently, while I was at fault, there was little point\nin blaming me, so she would let me off the hook... or so\nshe said.%K%P
虽然总觉得不太明白，\n不过，尽管是我的错，但责备我也无济于事了，\n看来她是不准备再追究下去了。%K%P
I didn't know if I should have felt grateful or concerned.%K%P
该说是谢天谢地呢，还是混乱不堪呢。%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dSo she's that caring landlord of yours, huh. At first it\ngave me such a shock I was barely able to talk.\d%K%P
「那个…是『爱照顾别人的房东小姐』吧。\n第一次看到她的时候，吓了我一跳呢」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI... only told you the truth.\d%K%P
「我…没说谎哦」%K%P
Well, I suppose I expected her to be surprised if she met\nher in person after a misleading introduction like that.%K%P
虽然我也觉得那种介绍方式，\n夏夜小姐见到她绝对会吃惊的。%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dShe seemed a bit hotheaded, but it looks like she's also\na cute, admirable kid that puts a hundred percent effort\ninto everything she does. ...Well, I'm sorry for saying\nall this after the fact.\d%K%P
「她看着有点冲动，但其实是个可爱又让人佩服的孩子，做什么事都会拼尽全力。\n……话说，我很抱歉现在才说这些。」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dHaha...\d%K%P
「哈哈…」%K%P
Talk about after the fact, indeed.%K%P
的确看上去很不自然。%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dWell, cheer up. I'm sure you'll make up when she cools\ndown a little.\d%K%P
「嘛，打起精神来吧。\n等她冷静下来后，很快就能和好的」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI can't just change how I feel in an instant.\d%K%P
「没那么简单啊…」%K%P
She might forgive me, but I wasn't sure I could forgive\nmyself.%K%P
就算她能原谅我，\n我能不能原谅自己又是另一个问题了。%K%P
It was precisely because she was such an admirable and\nforgiving girl who always pushed herself to the brink that\nI felt a deep-rooted anger at myself for always\ndisappointing her.%K%P
正因为她是认真、坚强、拼命的女孩，\n那么多次让她生气、失望、悲伤，\n反过来更会让我对自己感到生气、失望、悲伤的。%K%P
I thought I had finally gained the means to support her,\nyet it all fell apart in the blink of an eye -- and in the\nworst possible way, to boot.%K%P
而且现在的我…\n再一次失去本已得到了的，保护美都子的力量。%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dIf you think you need more time, I'm okay with you\nstaying here.\d%K%P
「看来要花点时间了，\n你在这里再多待一段时间也可以的哦」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI can't trouble you any longer.\d%K%P
「我不能再给你添麻烦了啊」%K%P
I was already at the stage where I was being called a\ngigolo.%K%P
现在，我给她添了够多的麻烦了，\n甚至都让自己被称作她的情夫了。%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dLook, when you say that things that don't actually cause\nme trouble are a trouble, it kinda makes me feel\ntroubled.\d%K%P
「不是麻烦硬说是麻烦，这才让我感到困扰」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI'm sorry...\d%K%P
「对不起…」%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dI kinda wish that you'd argue the point a bit.\d%K%P
「刚才我那句话是希望你吐槽的」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI'm sorry...\d%K%P
「十分抱歉…」%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\d...Hahh.\d%K%P
「…哈啊」%K%P
...Now that I thought about it, all those people who saw\nus in front of Ms. Kaya's door were probably suspecting\nall sorts of things.%K%P
…说起来，看见那阵骚动的公寓住户们，\n大概会对夏夜小姐产生无端的猜疑的吧。%K%P
I didn't leave the room for the past few days, so I was\nable to escape the prying eyes of the neighbors, but I\nguess this was it.%K%P
迄今为止，由于还没从房间走出过一步，\n所以能够避开邻居的视线，\n但到头来这个也化为了泡影。%K%P
It honestly felt like I carried a curse with me everywhere\nI went.%K%P
这么来想的话，\n也许最大的瘟神就是我啊。%K%P
I was the main cause for Mitoko's tears and Ms. Kaya's\nproblems.%K%P
让美都子感到悲伤，\n让夏夜小姐遭遇一个又一个麻烦。%K%P
I might very well have caused the bankruptcy of our\ncompany by the simple act of seeking employment there.%K%P
而且，公司倒闭，\n究其根源的话，就是作为瘟神的我进了公司…%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dI told you... to cheer up!\d%K%P
「所以说…打起精神来！」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dWh-What's that cold-- Whoa...?!\d%K%P
「好冷！？诶、呜哇！？」%K%P
I had only a moment to spend being surprised by the cold\nsensation of a beer can at my cheek.%K%P
一瞬间被碰到脸的冷罐子吓了一跳…%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dListen, Osamu. You can stay here for as long as you want.\nSo c'mon, calm down and start thinking straight.\d%K%P
「我说，理君。\n你可以尽情地待在这里哦？\n所以说放松一些冷静下来吧」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dH-How am I supposed to think straight in this position?!\d%K%P
「放、放、放松也不至于用这个姿势吧！」%K%P
Her arms -- still emanating some warmth from the shower\nshe took -- wrapped around my neck. I could smell the\nscent of shampoo and soap from her freshly washed hair and\nskin.%K%P
刚洗完澡的她用胳膊缠上我的脖子，\n阵阵温暖随之包围了我。湿湿的头发飘来香波的清爽。\n柔滑的皮肤散发着肥皂的迷香。%K%P
And then there was this soft sensation pressing against my\nback, that I... I...%K%P
最要命的是…\n压在我背部的、难以想象的柔软之物。%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dI'm having fun, so I'm genuinely okay with this. You can\nmove in here for real if you want.\d%K%P
「我也是很享受的，所以你不用在意。\n要不，正式搬出公寓来这里和我一起生活怎样？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dAre you even listening to me?!\d%K%P
「这都哪跟哪啊！？」%K%P
During all the time we spent together, we'd never been as\nclose as we were now.%K%P
三天里，我们住在同一个屋子里，而当下这一瞬\n我们两人的距离从各方面来说都达到最贴近的距离了。%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dI don't mind. We've lost our jobs, so I imagine it's\ngonna be tough to budget things for a while. With that in\nmind, saving some money by sharing an apartment doesn't\nsound like such a bad idea to me.\d%K%P
「我不介意哟。\n丢了工作，今后我们都会为钱而发愁吧，\n这样一起生活来减轻负担不也挺好的么？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI would mind!\d%K%P
「我介意！」%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\d...You can't relax with me?\d%K%P
「…和我一起，会喘不上气么？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dHow can I?!\d%K%P
「当然了！」%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dI didn't think I was putting that much pressure on you.\nAt least compared to your little landlord.\d%K%P
「我没有束缚你的打算哦。\n…至少，不会像房东小姐那样」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dRight now, I'm not talking about anyone in particular,\nbut common sense in general!\d%K%P
「我不是指特定的某个人而是一般论！」%K%P
The way she phrased that last line was a bit odd, but I\ndidn't want to lose track of the conversation again, so I\nignored it.%K%P
虽然我十分在意她后半句的嘀咕，\n但思索再三后还是选择了其它话题。%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dF-For example, let's say there's a very attractive young\nwoman, and one day, out of pity, she picks up a pathetic,\nuseless man and lets him stay in her room. Are you\nfollowing me so far?\d%K%P
「打、打个比方，这里有个非常有魅力的女性。\n她因为同情一个可怜的男人而将其收留了下来，\n让他待在自己的房间里。到这里没有问题吧？」%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dThat sounds like an awfully specific example.\d%K%P
「感觉你这一般论的场景限定还真是具体啊」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dBut either because she doesn't realize her own\nattractiveness or doesn't perceive the man as a member of\nthe other sex, she keeps acting in her room like she\nalways does, completely exposed and vulnerable.\d%K%P
「然而也许是没有注意到自己的魅力，\n也许是并没有把对方作为一个男人来看待，\n她依然像以往那样，毫无防备地行事」%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dDon't you think she's just trying to seduce him in her\nown way?\d%K%P
「那不就是在诱惑么？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...Is that so?\d%K%P
「………是那样么？」%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dAs long as we're discussing a hypothetical scenario, of\ncourse.\d%K%P
「终究是一般论吧」%K%P
%LCOsamu
